From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:55:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: read the charge of batteries that count energy.

Many laptop batteries put energy_full, energy_now and power_now in
sysfs, in microwatt-hours and microwatts, instead of charge_full,
charge_now and current_now.  Only the second were read, so such a
battery reported a capacity of 0, which GetSystemPowerStatus turned into
100 percent however full it was; and the battery percentage that
RegisterPowerSettingNotification tells of comes from the same place.

Checked against a sysfs tree of each kind: the same battery, half full
and discharging at 9.5W, reads 57020 of 28510 mWh at -9500 mW from
energy and 57000 of 28500 at -9462 from charge and voltage.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 13cd9f46cca1a8e44b15733f1684e6585395a0e1)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
index 3eee65e6036..3cde59acb59 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
@@ -4494,9 +4494,19 @@ static NTSTATUS fill_battery_state( SYSTEM_BATTERY_STATE *bs )
                 bs->Discharging = (strcmp(s, "Discharging\n") == 0);
                 bs->BatteryPresent = TRUE;
                 voltage = get_sys_int(path, "voltage_now");
-                bs->MaxCapacity = get_sys_int(path, "charge_full") * voltage / 1e9;
-                bs->RemainingCapacity = get_sys_int(path, "charge_now") * voltage / 1e9;
-                bs->Rate = -get_sys_int(path, "current_now") * voltage / 1e9;
+                if (get_sys_str(path, "energy_full", s))
+                {
+                    /* many batteries count microwatt-hours and microwatts instead */
+                    bs->MaxCapacity = get_sys_int(path, "energy_full") / 1000;
+                    bs->RemainingCapacity = get_sys_int(path, "energy_now") / 1000;
+                    bs->Rate = -get_sys_int(path, "power_now") / 1000;
+                }
+                else
+                {
+                    bs->MaxCapacity = get_sys_int(path, "charge_full") * voltage / 1e9;
+                    bs->RemainingCapacity = get_sys_int(path, "charge_now") * voltage / 1e9;
+                    bs->Rate = -get_sys_int(path, "current_now") * voltage / 1e9;
+                }
                 if (!bs->Charging && (LONG)bs->Rate < 0)
                     bs->EstimatedTime = 3600 * bs->RemainingCapacity / -(LONG)bs->Rate;
                 else
